        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="1118" n="1018" xml:id="pg1018"/>

                <head>No. 647.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Farman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Agency and Consulate-General of the United States at
                            Cairo</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-06-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 29, 1880</date>. (Received July
                        24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 416.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform, you that I sent
                    you on the 12th instant, from Alexandria, the following telegram: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush">Secretary <hi rendition="#small-caps">Evarts</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                        <p>Commander Gorringe sailed two o’clock to-day with obelisk. Will call at
                            Gibraltar.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">FARMAN.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>A telegraphic dispatch received on the 23d instant from the commander from
                    Gibaraltar informed me of his arrival at that place, and that everything was
                    working admirably well. The steamer was in good condition on her departure, and
                    I have no doubt will have arrived in New York before the receipt of this
                    dispatch.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. E. FARMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
